iltering when we perform  our pca analysis we see that and this is  in agreement with the published  study that the combination treatment  placed furthest from the vehicle control  group in both pcas  which shows its efficacy and also if you  look at  the horizontal component which shows the  most variation  in the data principle component one we  see that  treatment be that in both cases  contribute more  than mpa treatment to the combine effect  of bap and if you look at some of the  results  from that analysis if we look at the  lipid matrix  view in mpp in agreement with the paper  we see an increase  in in triangle glycerols from vehicle to  control  and it decreases in diastoles as we move  from vehicle control  vip treatment and what was different  from the paper was that we didn't  observe a significant  change in in in lies of  phosphatidylcholines or  lysophosphatidyl ethanol amines  and what was not measured in the paper  but what was measured in our study was  that a decrease  in phosphatidylcholine levels as you  move from control to ebip  treatment and also an increase in nine  hydroxyceramide levels  and an example to show the importance of  profiling approach in other words having  that  separation before mass spec we can look  at  this lipid uh matrix that just focus  focused on the nine hundred  9-hydroxyceramide  and we have a number of isomers that are  marked with asterisks there  and if you focus on one of them we see  that they had opposite trends  between vehicle and bap group and here  we are seeing their  uh overlaid eic's from profinder  and we see that lipid annotator  annotated their constituent levels based  on the difference  in in fragmentation pattern one had an  eighteen one twenty four one pattern and  the other eighteen twenty one four  zero and we see that the difference  between  these two uh fragments was s2  uh two six three and 261  representing one double bond or in other  words two hydrogen atoms and same goes  for  here three nine zero and three nine two  and and finally i would like to go back  to our untargeted lipidomics workflow  where we can annotate previously and  unannotated results  so here we change the horizontal axis in  our kendrick master effect plot  to a lipid class which can be done very  easily in mpp  and then we see that each lipid class  has their particular range for candid  mass defect  and this particular feature was not  annotated but it was highly differential  in statistical analysis  and that's why we wanted to annotate it  and we see there are three  uh lipid classes that that fall in the  range of this  mass defect uh as this an  unannotated feature and if we look at  the  zoom level and try uh  nine hydroxyceramide  [Music]  combinations and this can be done easily  with lipid calculator tool in lipid  annotator  we have found easily  this lipid structure which differs only  by 0.3 ppm  from our measured accurate bass and and  this can be a great way to to further  annotate structures  in our untargeted workflow  and with that i want to leave you with  our application notes that i have  mentioned during the slides and also  you can follow our linkedin page or our  omics webinar page on our agilent.com  website for  further updates and information on  comic studies with that thanks for your  time and you can have any questions

